<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- ========== IDENTITY ========== -->
    <Authors>The Geek Network</Authors>
    <Company>The Other Bhengu (PTY) Ltd</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2024-2025 The Other Bhengu (PTY) Ltd</Copyright>

    <!-- ========== VERSIONING ========== -->
    <Version>3.6.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>3.6.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>3.6.0.0</FileVersion>

    <!-- ========== LANGUAGE ========== -->
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

    <!-- ========== NUGET ========== -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/bhengubv/CircleAI</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/bhengubv/CircleAI</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>circle-ai;on-device-ai;llm;local-ai;circle;thegeeknetwork</PackageTags>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <!-- ========== BUILD QUALITY ========== -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>

    <!-- ========== PATH RESOLUTION ========== -->
    <PackageIconFullPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)assets\icon.png</PackageIconFullPath>
    <PackageReadmeFullPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)README.md</PackageReadmeFullPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ========== INCLUDED FILES (FIXED PATHS) ========== -->
    <None Include="$(PackageIconFullPath)" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Condition="Exists('$(PackageIconFullPath)')">
      <Visible>false</Visible>
    </None>
    <None Include="$(PackageReadmeFullPath)" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Condition="Exists('$(PackageReadmeFullPath)')">
      <Visible>false</Visible>
    </None>

    <!-- ========== PACKAGE REFERENCES ========== -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="1.1.1" PrivateAssets="All"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="9.0.0" PrivateAssets="All"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="ValidatePackageAssets" BeforeTargets="Pack">
    <Error Text="Required package icon not found at $(PackageIconFullPath)"
           Condition="!Exists('$(PackageIconFullPath)')"/>
    <Error Text="Required README not found at $(PackageReadmeFullPath)"
           Condition="!Exists('$(PackageReadmeFullPath)')"/>
  </Target>

  <!--
    ============================================================================
    ANDROID RELEASE SIGNING — the same block thegeeknetwork\code\Directory.Build.props
    uses for its seventeen apps, so every package this organisation ships is signed
    with one key and a person who already trusts one of them is not asked to trust a
    second identity for the engine behind it.

    IT WAS MISSING HERE AND NOTHING SAID SO. A Release Android build with no signing
    configured does not fail — `_ResolveAndroidSigningKey` falls back to the platform
    debug keystore — so both packages installed, ran, passed every suite, and could be
    uploaded nowhere. Confirmed on a P30 on 2026-10-01: both carried the debug
    signature.

    TWO DELIBERATE DIFFERENCES FROM THAT FILE, AND ONLY TWO:
      * No '$(UseMaui)' == 'true' gate. CircleAIService is a plain Microsoft.NET.Sdk
        Android project, not a MAUI one, so that condition would have left the half
        that holds the microphone and the models unsigned — the exact bug.
      * No <AndroidPackageFormat>aab</AndroidPackageFormat>. An app bundle is a Play
        Store artefact and this product is degoogled; a Release -t:Install of one also
        uninstalls first and takes the downloaded models with it. Both heads set apk
        for themselves and say why.

    WHERE THE KEY IS. Visual Studio keeps the one it manages at
    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Xamarin\Mono for Android\Keystore\TheGeekAlias\, and that copy is
    taken first: a machine with Visual Studio on it already has the key and needs no
    setup step at all. %USERPROFILE%\keystore\ is the fallback - where
    thegeeknetwork's Deployment\Setup-DeployMachine.ps1 puts it, and what its own
    props points at. Either resolves, and neither is copied.

    (An earlier edit of this comment lost a newline to a backslash at end of line,
    which is also how the publish flags broke the props load with MSB4024. A path
    ending in a separator is the last thing you want at the end of a line here.)

    Operator setup, once per machine:
      1. Nothing, if Visual Studio holds the keystore. Otherwise run
         Deployment\Setup-DeployMachine.ps1.
      2. setx ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS "<from the password manager>" - then a NEW SHELL.
      3. Verify: pwsh -c "[Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS','User')"

    Without it, Release fails at signing with XA4314 "$(AndroidSigningKeyPass) is
    empty". That is the right failure: a Release package signed with the debug key is
    the thing this block exists to stop.

    Release artefacts are produced the way thegeeknetwork\CLAUDE.md says, not by a
    build: `dotnet publish -f net10.0-android -m:1`. The -m:1 is mandatory — without
    it the publish runs out of memory — with no runtime identifier and not
    self-contained.
    ============================================================================
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="$(TargetFramework.Contains('-android')) AND '$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">
    <AndroidKeyStore>true</AndroidKeyStore>
    <_CircleAIVsKeystore>$(LOCALAPPDATA)\Xamarin\Mono for Android\Keystore\TheGeekAlias\TheGeekAlias.keystore</_CircleAIVsKeystore>
    <AndroidSigningKeyStore Condition="Exists('$(_CircleAIVsKeystore)')">$(_CircleAIVsKeystore)</AndroidSigningKeyStore>
    <AndroidSigningKeyStore Condition="'$(AndroidSigningKeyStore)' == ''">$(UserProfile)\keystore\TheGeekAlias.keystore</AndroidSigningKeyStore>
    <AndroidSigningKeyAlias>TheGeekAlias</AndroidSigningKeyAlias>
    <AndroidSigningKeyPass>$(ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS)</AndroidSigningKeyPass>
    <AndroidSigningStorePass>$(ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS)</AndroidSigningStorePass>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
